# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Without this file, a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true hands
# every worktree a CRLF working copy, while the agent tooling that edits these
# files writes LF. The content is identical and `git diff` is empty, but
# `git status` reports the files as modified anyway, in every worktree, forever.
# That was costing real attention: an agent opening a pane could not tell its own
# uncommitted work from the noise.
#
# Normalize to LF in the repository and in the working tree. The one exception is
# the Windows batch scripts, which stay CRLF: cmd.exe reads a batch file as it
# runs it, and LF-only line endings can break `goto` and label handling.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch wrappers must keep CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary, so Git never tries to translate them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated. Collapse them in diffs and keep them out of language stats.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
src-tauri/Cargo.lock -diff linguist-generated
